(1739245, 232888, 15711, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>Upon first view of this my first thought is that the focal point of the shot is in shadow.  Maybe that was your intent, as it is a gravyard and the sun has already set on its inhabitants.  BUT, it does make it difficult to appreciate the texture and variation of color. I think you could achieve that same goal with the use of possibly a sepia filter, to denote an old nostalgic sense yet have the light coming from a different angle.  The perspective is good. The angle from which you see the church is interesting and the various shapes work this way versus being shot straight on. The composition is good and I like the single tree to the left as a grounding force which also serves as a semi-frame. Keep up the good work.  All the best, Judy</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! Upon first view of this my first thought is that the focal point of the shot is in shadow.  Maybe that was your intent, as it is a gravyard and the sun has already set on its inhabitants.  BUT, it does make it difficult to appreciate the texture and variation of color. I think you could achieve that same goal with the use of possibly a sepia filter, to denote an old nostalgic sense yet have the light coming from a different angle.  The perspective is good. The angle from which you see the church is interesting and the various shapes work this way versus being shot straight on. The composition is good and I like the single tree to the left as a grounding force which also serves as a semi-frame. Keep up the good work.  All the best, Judy', '2005-09-26 09:24:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1739253, 233039, 16148, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on another winning image!  Always nice to see original ideas at the top.</td>', 'Congratulations on another winning image!  Always nice to see original ideas at the top.', '2005-09-26 09:32:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1739254, 232461, 15711, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>I think this has definite potential! The orangey red tones of the track leading into the orangey pink sky give a sense of continuity. The perspective is good and the leading line sense of it does exactly what the title denotes. I wish that the clarity was a bit sharper, which is hard to attain with limited lighting. Maybe the use of the unsharp mask could help do this. The misty background is an appealing aspect to the shot and lends itself to an ethereal feel to it. The white touch of cloud in the sky at the top of the shot in the background is a nice added touch. There isn''t alot of contrast but that is to be expected with the time of day and the look I think you were going for.  Overall a nice image that might use a touch of tweaking here and there to really make it a prize winner..    Take care, Judy</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! I think this has definite potential! The orangey red tones of the track leading into the orangey pink sky give a sense of continuity. The perspective is good and the leading line sense of it does exactly what the title denotes. I wish that the clarity was a bit sharper, which is hard to attain with limited lighting. Maybe the use of the unsharp mask could help do this. The misty background is an appealing aspect to the shot and lends itself to an ethereal feel to it. The white touch of cloud in the sky at the top of the shot in the background is a nice added touch. There isn''t alot of contrast but that is to be expected with the time of day and the look I think you were going for.  Overall a nice image that might use a touch of tweaking here and there to really make it a prize winner..    Take care, Judy', '2005-09-26 09:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
